# Mainspring — server configuration
#
# Copy to backend/.env and fill in. Nothing in here belongs in the repository:
# .env is in .gitignore and must stay there.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database --
MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
MYSQL_PORT=3306
MYSQL_USER=mainspring
MYSQL_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_DB=mainspring

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ server --
# Public sign-up. On a reachable server this belongs at false, otherwise
# anybody can make themselves an account.
ALLOW_SIGNUP=false

# Debugging only: switches authentication off entirely, for the API and the
# socket. Never on a server anybody else can reach.
# GUEST_MODE=true

# Set when the server sits behind a reverse proxy, so the login rate limit
# counts visitors rather than counting the proxy as one visitor.
# TRUST_PROXY=true

# Comma-separated, only needed when the frontend is served from somewhere
# else than the API.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mainspring.example.com

# ------------------------------------------------------- Google calendars --
# Reading each employee's Google calendar, one way, with a Workspace service
# account. Leave everything below unset and the feature stays off — no link
# can be configured and nothing is fetched.
#
# Why a service account and not the usual "connect your account" button:
# Google only accepts https redirect URIs for web OAuth clients, and an
# installation that lives behind a VPN has no https name it could register.
# Domain-wide delegation needs no redirect at all.
#
# Setting it up, once, by a Workspace SUPER admin. Menu labels are the German
# ones, because that is what the consoles show here; checked in August 2026.
#
#   1. console.cloud.google.com -> "Projekt erstellen".
#   2. "APIs & Dienste" -> "Bibliothek" -> "Google Calendar API" -> aktivieren.
#      Nothing else: this integration reads calendars and does no more.
#   3. "IAM und Verwaltung" -> "Dienstkonten" -> "Dienstkonto erstellen".
#      Roles and access can be left empty — the permission that matters is
#      granted in step 5, not here.
#   4. Open the service account -> tab "Schlüssel" -> "Schlüssel hinzufügen"
#      -> "Neuen Schlüssel erstellen" -> JSON. The file downloads once.
#
#      There is NO "domainweite Delegierung" switch on the service account any
#      more. Google removed it; the authorisation now happens entirely in the
#      admin console, in the next step. If you were looking for that checkbox:
#      it is gone, and it is not needed.
#
#   5. admin.google.com -> Menü -> "Sicherheit" -> "Zugriffs- und
#      Datenkontrolle" -> "API-Steuerung" -> "Domainweite Delegierung
#      verwalten" -> "Neu hinzufügen".
#        Client-ID:     the NUMBER, not the address. It is the field
#                       "client_id" in the JSON from step 4, and it is also
#                       shown on the service account as "Eindeutige ID".
#        OAuth-Bereiche: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
#      Allow a few minutes before it takes effect.
#   6. Put the JSON key somewhere outside the repository and point the
#      variable below at it.
#   7. In Mainspring: Administration -> Team, enter each colleague's Google
#      address. The address must be a user of the domain.
#
# If "API-Steuerung" is missing, the account is not a super admin — a normal
# admin does not see it. If there is no admin console at all, the domain is
# not on Google Workspace, and this whole mechanism does not apply; see
# HANDOVER for the iCal fallback.
#
# The key file is the credential for reading every calendar in the domain.
# Treat it like the database password.
# GOOGLE_SA_KEY_FILE=/etc/mainspring/google-service-account.json

# Instead of the file, if you prefer variables. The private key is a PEM with
# newlines in it; write them as \n and keep the quotes.
# GOOGLE_SA_CLIENT_EMAIL=mainspring-calendar@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# GOOGLE_SA_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIE…\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# How often the background sync runs, in minutes. 0 switches the timer off —
# which is what a second instance of the server wants, so that two processes
# do not fetch the same calendars.
# GOOGLE_SYNC_MINUTES=15
